<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20086] sanity test_56ob aarch64: 'lfs find /mnt/lustre/d56ob.sanity -mtime 2w' wrong: found 0, expected 1</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20086</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;This issue was created by maloo for Andreas Dilger &amp;lt;adilger@thelustrecollective.com&amp;gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This issue relates to the following test suite run:&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/0109704a-3fe0-446d-bb20-682162328694" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/0109704a-3fe0-446d-bb20-682162328694&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;test_56ob failed with the following error:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;'/usr/bin/lfs find /mnt/lustre/d56ob.sanity -mtime 2w' wrong: found 0, expected 1
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Test session details:&lt;br/&gt;
clients: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/123340" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/123340&lt;/a&gt; - 5.14.0-503.40.1.el9_5.aarch64+64k&lt;br/&gt;
servers: &lt;a href="https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/123340" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://build.whamcloud.com/job/lustre-reviews/123340&lt;/a&gt; - 4.18.0-553.89.1.el8_lustre.x86_64&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This is failing several times per week, with different time ranges (e.g. &lt;tt&gt;-mtime 1d&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;-mtime 4h&lt;/tt&gt;, &lt;tt&gt;-mtime -1y&lt;/tt&gt;) so it doesn't appear to be a small race with the timestamps, but something more fundamental like not finding files at all, or the timestamps not being set correctly.  The problem happens exclusively on aarch64 or aarch64+64k clients.  There are some other failures of test_56ob on x86_64 clients but they are caused by unrelated problems in the patches being tested (errors creating files or setting timestamps).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;VVVVVVV DO NOT REMOVE LINES BELOW, Added by Maloo for auto-association VVVVVVV&lt;br/&gt;
sanity test_56ob - '/usr/bin/lfs find /mnt/lustre/d56ob.sanity -mtime 2w' wrong: found 0, expected 1&lt;/p&gt;</description>
